    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py`, keeping the `UnsafePathError(ValueError)` class and the function signature from the stub. The function validates `dest`, strips trailing `/` from it, and splits each member on both `/` and `\\`. It drops empty and `.` segments and pops on `..`, raising `UnsafePathError` for NUL characters, leading `/` or `\\`, ASCII drive prefixes like `C:` (checked before splitting), any `..` that climbs above the destination, and members that are empty after normalisation. Directory entries (names ending in a separator) are validated but left out of the result. File members whose normalised paths collide case-insensitively raise `UnsafePathError`. The function returns `base + \"/\" + rel` for each file in input order, so `dest=\"/\"` yields `/name`. Nothing was run or tested, since shell access was not available, and I wrote no other files.",
